   UNGC independent-distance set: rms z 0.473 vs SPARC's 0.236 (ratio 2.01); at s = 0.43 dex that set would need N = 1755 (it has 350) for sigma_beta = 0.05; it has no rotation curves (W50 only), so it is a lever-arm census, not an a0 sample
D2 other repo tables: KT2017 galaxies (HRV only, no distances); KT2017 groups_full (group distances from flow/TF: circular); 2MRS (cz only); ALFALFA tables (flow-model distances: circular); SLACS/SLUGGS/ATLAS3D (ellipticals, not the SPARC a0 estimator).  None gives a redshift-independent-distance sample beyond ~40 Mpc with rotation curves.
D3 lever-arm ceiling: half the sample at w = 0 and half at 1000 km/s gives z in {0, 2.78}: rms z = 1.39; sigma_u = H0 e_D <= 100 km/s needs D <= 30 Mpc at e_D/D = 5% and D <= 49 Mpc at 3%
D3 but nearby galaxies co-move with the Local Volume (r(u, V_LG.n) = 0.75 in SPARC): u ~ V_LG.n, so w = 0 relative to the CMB frame is rare inside 40 Mpc; the single component u alone cannot give the 3D w (only 3D flow reconstructions can)
D4 STATEMENT: SPARC-like N = 68 gives sigma_beta ~ 0.45 (Fisher); a diagnostic sample (sigma_beta <= 0.05) needs N * rms(z)^2 >= (ln10 s / 0.05)^2 = 392 for s = 0.43 dex, i.e. ~392 galaxies with independent distances to ~5% and w spanning 0-1000 km/s (rms z ~ 1), or ~85 if per-galaxy a0 scatter s could be cut to 0.2 dex; no repo table supplies it.
